# Surviving mutants each package may carry, enforced by
# internal/tools/mutate in the scheduled Mutation workflow.
#
# A mutant is one small change to the code — a comparison swapped, a
# negation dropped, a 0 turned into a 1 — that the package's own tests
# did not notice. Each survivor is either a missing assertion or a change
# with no observable effect, and the ceiling exists because the second
# kind cannot be driven to zero: an error check that only decides whether
# a debug line is logged, a comparison the enclosing condition already
# settled, a guard the next line repeats. The commonest shape of all —
# the zero Go returns beside an error — is not mutated at all, so it never
# reaches this ceiling.
#
# Lowering a ceiling in a pull request that asserts more is welcome.
# Raising one is a decision to argue for in the pull request body, the
# way .coverage-floor is: the number says how much of this package's
# behaviour is nailed down, and it may not quietly go up.
#
# Every package listed here is run in full, so this file is also the
# scope: a package joins the run by being declared, with a measured
# ceiling attached.
internal/evidence 12
# internal/adapter measured 2026-09-27 at 115 mutants, 105 caught. The ten
# survivors are four shapes: seven error checks that decide nothing but
# whether a debug line is logged; a channel buffer where both paths receive
# exactly once; a `> 0` widened to `>= 0`, where the branch it then takes
# does what the branch it skipped would have done; and a constant whose
# mutated form is the same number once the integer division truncates.
#
# It was 15 before, and the scheduled run of 2026-09-21 met that exactly:
# fifteen survivors against fifteen allowed, no margin at all. Protocol
# negotiation (#354, four days later) added the branch that sends the probe
# at the floor, nothing asserted the version on the wire, and the count
# went to 16 — so a ceiling with no room left was spent by the next feature
# that touched the package, which is the argument for lowering one as far
# as the measurement allows rather than to the first number that passes.
#
# The number also moved, which is worse than a number that is too high.
# Two copies of one verdict sat in branches a race chose between, so the
# same tree reported 16 survivors or 17 depending on which copy the tests
# reached — and 2026-09-21's run caught in CI what this machine did not.
# wait() keeps one copy of the sentence now.
internal/adapter  10
spec/evidence      1
# internal/manifest decides whether a drill is refused, and its failure
# mode is silent acceptance: a comparison inverted here passes every
# corrupt artifact, while coverage stays green because the line still
# ran. Measured 2026-09-25 at 60 mutants, 57 caught. The three survivors
# are one shape — the zero returned beside a fault, which every caller
# discards after checking the fault.
internal/manifest  3
# internal/checks decides every verdict a record carries, and its failure
# mode is a check that passes on something it never looked at. Measured
# 2026-09-27 at 68 mutants, 64 caught. The four survivors are two shapes:
# the clamp that keeps a future timestamp from printing a negative age,
# whose every boundary vanishes under the detail's truncation to seconds,
# and an empty environment map allocated instead of left nil, which
# behaves identically downstream.
#
# Joining the run cost three real assertions rather than none. DialectFrom
# — the conversion that carries an adapter's declarations into a check —
# had no direct test at all, because the suite built Dialects by hand; the
# row_count bounds were never tested at their inclusive edges; and the
# freshness clamp for a timestamp ahead of the drill host's clock was
# unasserted.
internal/checks     4
# Still outside the run, measured 2026-09-27 so the next pass starts from
# facts rather than from a survey: internal/config at 145 mutants, 130
# caught, 14 survived — half of them in gameday.go, which is its own
# feature area; and internal/core, unmeasured. Both decide what a record
# says, so both belong here eventually. Each joins in its own change,
# because joining costs assertions rather than a line in this file.
